node_modules/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
# Scratch space for anything a script renders for a human to look at — the
# installer-art previews, and the injected scripts the dialog test dumps for
# `node --check`. Never an input to a build.
target/
# Staged by scripts/bundle-runtime.mjs: the Node runtime and dsh the installer
# ships. The directory itself is tracked so the bundler's glob always matches —
# a build without a staged runtime falls back to `dsh` on PATH.
src-tauri/resources/*
!src-tauri/resources/.gitkeep
# Not staged: source, which happens to live where the resources go so that one
# path serves both a bundled build and `tauri dev`. See src-tauri/src/plugins.rs.
!src-tauri/resources/preset-plugins.json
# The installer's sidebar and header bitmaps, drawn from the app icon by
# scripts/make-installer-art.mjs. Generated rather than committed: a .bmp is a
# blob nobody can review, and the icon they are made from is already tracked.
# Not under resources/, because that glob is copied into the installation
# directory and these are only read while the installer is built.
src-tauri/installer/
bash.exe.stackdump
